{
  "note": "Electrical switchgear and sources the asset source lacks (issue #38). The plant design draws both SPPA incomers and all three gensets of a side straight into the MSB main bus meter (edges labelled TX-n and ATS-A/B), and MSB A_1 and B_9 both straight into the L1 DB incomer (labelled ATS-DB), which would parallel utility with gensets and side A with side B. The changeover equipment that sits in the MSB and L1 DB switchgear is added as unexported ATS assets (~ATS-A, ~ATS-B, ~ATS-DB) wired normal/emergency/load, with their transfer, genset start and load shed sequences as control bindings. Each utility incomer is fed by an unexported Utility Supply (~TX-1..4: grid plus 5 MVA transformer, plant-design basis.capacities), so a transformer or incomer loss is a fault on that one asset. The standalone demo rack gets its own incomer (~DEMO-RACK-SUPPLY, 100 kVA assumed).",
